--- A loop's variable named like a name bound before the loop hides it
--- inside the loop only: after the loop the name is what it was, in both
--- modes. (Compiled, a top-level record named like a later loop's variable
--- had been declared a record or none, and the program did not build.)
struct P [x, y]
a = P[1, [10, 20]]
c = a
c.y[0] = 99
log[c.y]
lens = for c in range[3]
    c * 2
log[lens]
for c in range[2]
    log[c + 1]
log[c.x]
